GitHub CoPilot Controls

Control ID: COP-01
Control Name: CoPilot Seat Assignments 
Category: Access Control

The IT/Security team implements COP-01 by restricting GitHub CoPilot seat assignments exclusively to developers who have submitted an approved access request through the IT service management system. The organization uses GitHub Enterprise Admin Center to provision and deprovision CoPilot seats, tied directly to role-based eligibility. This occurs at the time of onboarding, role change, or upon an approved request. Results are reviewed by the IT Manager and Security team on a quarterly basis to identify and remove unused or unauthorized seats. Evidence includes GitHub Enterprise seat assignment reports, access request tickets, quarterly access review sign-off documentation, and offboarding checklists confriming seat revocation.

this maps directly to NIST SP 800-53 AC-2
-------------------------------------------
Control ID: COP-02
Control Name: Privileged Access for CoPilot Admins
Category: Access Management

The Security Team implements COP-02 by limiting GitHub CoPilot admin rights to a designated group of GitHub Enterprise administrators. The organization uses GitHub role-based permissions to seperate admin from standard user access. This occurs at initial setup and reviewed annually. Results are reviewed by the CISO. Evidence includes admin role assignment logs and access review sign-offs.

NIST 800-53 AC-6 - Least Privilege
-------------------------------------------
Control ID: COP-03
Control Name: CoPilot Access Revocation on Termination
Category: Access Management 

The HR Team implements COP-03 by ensuring CoPilot seat revocation is included in the employee offboarding checklist within 24 hours of termination. The organization uses automated deprovisioning tied to HR system triggers where possible. This occurs upon every employee or contractor seperation. Results are reviewed by IT Security monthly. Evidence includes offboarding tickets, seat revocation confirmation logs, and HR termination records.

NIST 800-53: PS-4 - Personnel Termination
-------------------------------------------
Control ID: COP-04
Control Name: Data Sharing Opt-Out
Category: Data Protection

The Security Team implements COP-04 by disabling GitHub's use of organizational code for AI model training through enterprise policy settings. The organization uses GitHub Enterprise policy controls to enforce opt-out across all users. This occurs at initial platform configuration. Results are reviewed by Legal and Privacy teams annually. Evidence includes GitHub enterprise policy screenshots and DPA confirmation from GitHub.

NIST 800-53: SI-12 - Information Management and Retention
-------------------------------------------
Control ID: COP-05
Control Name: Source Code Exclusion Policy
Category: Data Protection

The Securitty Team implements COP-05 by configuring CoPilot content exclusions to block suggestions from repositories containing senstive data, PII, or regualted infromation. The organization uses GitHub at the enterprise level. This occurs at initial deployment and reviewed quarterly by the Data Protection Officer. Evidence includes content exclusion configuration exports nad repository classification records.

NIST 800-53: SC-28 - Protection of Information at Rest
-------------------------------------------
Control ID: COP-06
Control Name: AI Output Accountability Policy
Category: Human Oversight

The AI Governance team implements COP-06 by establishing a policy that developers are fully accountable for any CoPilot-generated code they accept and commit. The organization uses developer policy acknowledgment and onbaording training to enforce this standard. This occurs at CoPilot onboarding and annually. Results are reviewed by the AI Governance Lead. Evidence includes signed policy acknowledgments and training completion records.

NIST 800-53: PL-4 Rules of Behavior
-------------------------------------------
Control ID: COP-07
Control Name: Mandatory Review of AI-Generated Code
Category: Human Oversight

Engineering Lead implements COP-07 by requiring all CoPilot-assisted code to pass at least one human peer review before merging into protected branches. The organization uses GitHub branch protection rules with required reviewers enforced at the repository level. This occurs on every pull request. Results are reviewed by Engineering Managers monthly. Evidence includes PR approval history, branch protection rule configurations, and merge logs.

NIST 800-53: SA-11 - Developer Testing and Evaluation
-------------------------------------------
Control ID: COP-08
Control Name: CoPilot Usage Reporting
Category: Monitoring

The IT Team implements COP-08 by producing a monthly CoPilot usage reporting summarizing active users, seat utilization, policy violations, and flagged events for leadership review. The organization uses GitHub Enterprise usage dashboards and SIEM exports to compile the report. This occurs monthly. Results are reviewed by the CISO and IT Director. Evidence includes monthly report artifacts, distribution records, and leadership acknowledgment.

NIST 800-53: AU-6 - Audit Record Review Analysis
-------------------------------------------
Control ID: COP-09
Control Name: Data Processing Agreement Review
Category: Third-Party Risk

The Legal team implements COP-09 by ensuring a current Data Processing Agreement (DPA) with GitHub is executed and covers CoPilot's AI data handling obligations before platform approval. The organization uses a contract management system to track DPA status and renewal dates. This occurs before go-live and at each contract renewal. Results are reviewed by the DPO. Evidence includes signed DPA, contract management records, and legal sign-off.

NIST 800-53: SA-4 - Aquisition Process
-------------------------------------------
Control ID: COP-10
Control Name: AI Bias and Output Quality Review
Category: Responsible AI

The Engineering team implements COP-10 by sampling CoPilot suggestions across repositories to assess output quality, potential bias in code patterns, and adherence to secure coding standards. The organization uses manual sampling and static analysis tooling to evaluate suggestion quality. This occurs quarterly. Results are reviewed by the AI Governace committee. Evidence includes sampling reports, static analysis results, and committee review records.

NIST 800-53: SI-7 - Software, Firmware, and Information Integrity
-------------------------------------------
Control ID: COP-11
Control Name: Developer AI Literacy Training 
Category: Responsible AI

The AI Governace team implements COP-11 by requiring all CoPilot users to complete AI Literacy Training covering responsible use, limitations of AI-generated code, and security risks before seat activation. The organization uses an LMS to assign, track, and enforce training completion. This occurs before initial access and annually. Results are reviewed by the AI Governance lead. Evidence includes LMS completion records, training content documentation, and seat provisioning confirmation.

NIST 800-53: AT-2 - Literacy Training and Awareness
-------------------------------------------
Control ID: COP-12
Control Name: CoPilot-Related Security Event Reporting 
Category: Incident Response 

Developers implement COP-12 by reporting any suspected AI-generated code vulnerability, data leak, or policy violation through the organization's established security incident reporting channel within 24 hours of discovery. The organization uses the ITSM ticketing system with an AI-specific incident category to capture and route reports. This occurs upon discovery of any qualifying event. Results are reviewed by the IR team. Evidence includes incident tickets, response timelines, and resolution records.

NIST 800-53: IR-6 - Incident Reporting
-------------------------------------------
Control ID: COP-13
Control Name: Regulatory Applicability Assessment
Category: Compliance and Regulatory Requirements

The Compliance team implements COP-13 by conducting a pre-deployment regulatory applicability assessment to determine which data protection and AI regulations apply to CoPilot use. The organization uses a compliance matrix mapped to CoPilot's data flows. This occurs before go-live and reviewed annually. Results are reviewed by the General Counsel. Evidence includes the completed assessment, compliance matrix, and legal sign-off.

NIST 800-53: PL-1 - Policy and Procedures
-------------------------------------------
Control ID: COP-14
Control Name: AI Feature Enablement Approval Process
Category: Model Governance

The AI Governance team implements COP-14 by requiring formal risk assessment and approval before enabling new or experimental CoPilot features beyond the approval baseline. The organization uses a lightweight AI feature approval workflow in the ITSM platform. This occurs before any new feature is activated in the production environment. Results are reviewed by the CISO and AI Governance lead. Evidence includes feature approval requests, risk assessments, and approval records.

NIST 800-53: CM-4 - Impact Analyses
-------------------------------------------
Control ID: COP-15
Control Name: User Communication for CoPilot Updates
Category: Change Management

The Engineering team implements COP-15 by notifying all CoPilot users of material platform updates, policy changes, or new feature activations at least 5 business days in advance. The organization uses internal communication channels (email,Slack) to distribute change notices. This occurs before every material change. Results are reviewed by Engineering Leadership. Evidence includes communication records, distribution lists, and acknowledgment logs.

